# Zapp sibling repository dependency lockfile.
# CI verifies that the checked-out zappMessaging SHA matches before building.
# Update when intentionally bumping a sibling dependency.

# The published SDK, whose history is squashed and so carries its own commit ids:
# this repository pins the mirror, not the development repo it is published from.
# GitHub: https://github.com/JustZappIt/zappmessaging-sdk
zappMessaging=a8b88ed4f6cc22382a4c79167340031aa12c42b1

# bare-kit is a direct clone of holepunchto/bare-kit v2.0.0 with no Zapp modifications.
# GitHub: https://github.com/holepunchto/bare-kit
# The local ../bare-kit/ directory has no git history; CI checks out the pinned commit.
# Update both this SHA and the workflow ref when upgrading bare-kit.
bare-kit=15a3569f3d704de7151761051c8d9cc2e299414f

# zcash-android-wallet-sdk is resolved from Maven snapshots, not includeBuild: upstream
# zodl ships SDK_INCLUDED_BUILD_PATH blank and requests ZCASH_SDK_VERSION from the
# central.sonatype.com snapshot repo, so we match it rather than building the Rust backend
# locally. This SHA is the provenance of that artifact, not a build input; CI does not
# verify it.
#
# NOW ON v3.1.0-SNAPSHOT, for coinholder polling: it is the first published snapshot with the
# public VotingSdk facade and a native library built with cfg(zcash_voting) (63 voting JNI
# symbols; 3.0.1 exports none). It is ALSO the first snapshot without the ZODL Slipstream sync
# engine and the isSlipstreamEnabled WalletCoordinator parameter, which v3.0.0/v3.0.1 carried
# alongside the OrchardMigrationSdk. The two features do not coexist in any published artifact.
# Voting is therefore behind VOTING_ENABLED=false and this trade is unresolved -- do not ship
# either half without settling it. See docs/voting.md.
#
# Upstream did not drop Slipstream by accident: SDK commit 6b4d6339 "MOB-1757: Remove the
# Slipstream sync engine and its AGPL dependency" removes it because the zodl-slipstream crate
# is AGPL-3.0-only while the SDK publishes MIT artifacts, and adds a cargo-deny licence gate to
# keep it out. Zapp is itself AGPL-3.0-only, so that specific conflict does not bind us -- but
# keeping Slipstream now means maintaining a permanent fork of the SDK's native build against
# an upstream licence gate, not just pinning an older snapshot.
#
# PROVENANCE SHA BELOW IS STALE: it is v3.0.1's. The published 3.1.0-20260820.161424-1 does not
# match 6b4d6339 either (it still exports syncBurst/syncToTip, which that commit deletes), so
# the exact source commit is unverified. Establish it during the SDK decision.
#
# GitHub: https://github.com/zcash/zcash-android-wallet-sdk
zcashAndroidWalletSdk=b5a302cbbe6dd3da4a615dade221ca3461236304
